From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: ExplorerBrowser FillFromObject and RemoveAll, the results folder (3706)

shell32: ExplorerBrowser FillFromObject and RemoveAll, the results folder

FillFromObject makes the browser show a results folder, an IShellFolder2
whose items are the id lists it was given: from an IDataObject (shell id
list), an IShellItemArray, an IShellItem (a folder gives its children) or an
IShellFolder. Each item is asked about its name, attributes, columns, menus
and data object from the folder it really lives in. With
EBF_SELECTFROMDATAOBJECT the peers of the data object's items are shown and
only its items are selected. Further calls add items, the folder implements
IResultsFolder (AddItem, AddIDList, RemoveItem, RemoveIDList, RemoveAll, the
view follows), RemoveAll empties it (E_UNEXPECTED before a fill), and
browsing elsewhere leaves it; EBO_NAVIGATEONCE keeps the browser in it.
